  "_comment": "SALVAGE kit: the kill tally, and a FLAT decal like the hazard band - a thin steel sheet with two GENERATIONS of marks on it that disagree about which way is straight. The old tally was painted over with a soot block yawed 9 degrees, and two rust marks still peek out past its edge; the fresh tally - four green bars and the strike-through of a five-count - is yawed 4 degrees the OTHER way, in the same livery green the patches are cut from, because a raider paints with the paint it has. Everything under 0.03 of a cell tall, so the piece lies on anything: this is the kit's second thin-shape carrier and its rule asks for no seat and no depth.",
